date: 2026-10-25
categories: til
---

t-score is the metric used to measure bone density. it is actually just the standard deviation from the mean human bone density. a t score of > -1 is ok. -1 to -2.5 is osteoponia and <-2.5 is osteoporosis.

ossification is the biological process of forming new bone cells/tissues. this is done by specialised cells called osteoblasts. there are also cells called osteoclasts which reabsorb or break down micro-broken bone tissue. 

bone density increases until late 20s, when it peaks and then declines. so it is a good precation to have good bone density peak.

